{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-002", "approach": "LEX5", "approach_base": "LEX5", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Douglass first learned the alphabet from Mrs. Auld, but Mr. Auld stopped the lessons, and Douglass finished learning to read by making friends with little white boys in the street who taught him.\n\n- Mrs. Auld kindly began teaching him the A, B, C and to spell words of three or four letters (Chapter VI).\n- Mr. Auld found out and forbade her to continue, saying it was unlawful and unsafe to teach a slave to read (Chapter VI).\n- He argued that learning would spoil a slave and forever unfit him to be a slave, and that \"if you give a nigger an inch, he will take an ell\" (Chapter VI).\n- Douglass said the \"inch\" had already been given, so no precaution could stop him from taking the \"ell\" (Chapter VII).\n- He converted little white boys he met in the street into teachers, took his book on errands, and traded bread for lessons, finally succeeding in learning to read (Chapter VII).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 1011 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o011", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b109", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [76319, 77330], "meta": {"chunk": 5734, "completed": 14, "prefix": 0}}, {"text": "[stripped: 1027 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o012", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b115", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b116"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [84391, 85418], "meta": {"chunk": 5746, "completed": 140, "prefix": 0}}, {"text": "[stripped: 886 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en",